# The deliverable is source code, requirements.txt and README.md — nothing else.
# Everything is excluded by default and the deliverable is let back in below, so a
# file added later is out until somebody says otherwise, rather than in until
# somebody notices.

*

# Git has to be allowed into a directory before anything inside it can be let back
# in: a file under an excluded directory cannot be re-included.
!*/

# …except these, which are never descended into whatever they hold. The leading
# slash anchors them to the repository root: written bare, `logs/` would also
# swallow any folder of that name under `src/`.
/logs/
/.venv/
/venv/
/env/
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# --- the deliverable ------------------------------------------------------------
!.gitignore
!README.md
!requirements.txt
!app.py

# Source: the pages, the modules behind them, and the tests over the core.
!**/*.py

# The two files the source cannot start without: the sidebar logo `app.py` loads,
# and the theme Streamlit reads before the first line of the app runs.
!assets/*.svg
!.streamlit/config.toml

# The three season CSVs. Not source, but the brief asks for `pip install` then
# `streamlit run app.py` to work on a fresh clone, and they are the app's only
# source of data — a repository that cannot start is not a deliverable. Read-only:
# nothing in the app ever writes here, so nothing new appears in this folder.
!data/*.csv

# --- deliberately out -----------------------------------------------------------
# An empty leftover at the root, kept out of the submission.
/main.py
# Working notes and the French reading copy of the README — neither is the deliverable.
README.fr.md
# The brief itself.
*.docx
